## Koide in V_4 form

### Derivation of the equivalent V_4 ratio

The Koide constraint `K = Σm/(Σ√m)² = 2/3` rearranges to:

    (Σ √m_obs)²  =  (3/2) · Σ m_obs

Substituting into the V_4 trivial component:

    |w_χ_0|²  =  (Σ √m_obs)² / 4  =  (3/2 · Σ m_obs) / 4  =  (3/8) · |w|²

And:

    |w_⊥V_4|²  =  |w|² − |w_χ_0|²  =  (5/8) · |w|²

Therefore:

    |w_χ_0|² : |w_⊥V_4|²  =  3 : 5

### Substrate primitives in this ratio

The two integers `3` and `5` are framework primitives:

| Framework primitive | Value | Identity in V_4 ratio |
|---|---|---|
| `q_3` (color triplet count) | 3 | Numerator of |w_χ_0|² fraction |
| `MEDIANT = q_2 + q_3` (DM logit numerator) | 5 | Numerator of |w_⊥V_4|² fraction |
| Sum: `q_3 + MEDIANT = 2 q_2 + q_3 = 2 + 6 = 8 = q_2³ = k_quark` | 8 | Denominator |

The denominator `q_2³ = q_2 + 2 q_3 = 8` is the SU(3) adjoint
dimension (`mass_sector_closure.md` Theorem). The numerators
`q_3` and `MEDIANT` are foundational substrate primitives.

### Numerical verification (PDG)

| Quantity | PDG value | Substrate prediction | Match |
|---|---|---|---|
| `|w_χ_0|² / |w|²` | `0.375005` | `q_3/q_2³ = 3/8 = 0.375000` | 0.002% |
| `|w_⊥V_4|² / |w|²` | `0.624995` | `MEDIANT/q_2³ = 5/8 = 0.625000` | 0.001% |
| `|w_χ_0|² / |w_⊥V_4|²` | `0.600012` | `q_3/MEDIANT = 3/5 = 0.600000` | 0.002% |

Match to substrate primitive ratio is at the precision of the
Koide constraint itself (which holds to ~10⁻⁵ on PDG data).

